      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. \n\nStep 1: Prime factorization of 91\n91 can be divided by 7, so we have 91 = 7 × 13.\n\nStep 2: List all the positive divisors\nSince 91 is a product of two prime numbers, its divisors are 1, 7, 13, and 91.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the sum of the divisors\nTo find the sum of these divisors, we simply add them together: 1 + 7 + 13 + 91 = 112.\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is \\boxed{112}.",
