      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can see that 91 can be factored as follows:\n\n91 = 7 × 13\n\nNow, we can use the formula for finding the sum of divisors of a number based on its prime factorization. If a number N has the prime factorization N = p₁^a₁ × p₂^a₂ × ... × pₙ^aₙ, then the sum of all positive divisors of N is given by:\n\nSum = (p₁^(a₁ + 1) - 1)/(p₁ - 1) × (p₂^(a₂ + 1) - 1)/(p₂ - 1) × ... × (pₙ^(aₙ + 1) - 1)/(pₙ - 1)\n\nIn our case, N = 91, p₁ = 7, a₁ = 1, p₂ = 13, a₂ = 1. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\nSum = (7^(1 + 1) - 1)/(7 - 1) × (13^(1 + 1) - 1)/(13 - 1)\nSum = (7² - 1)/(6) × (13² - 1)/(12)\nSum = (49 - 1)/6 × (169 - 1)/12\nSum = 48/6 × 168/12\nSum = 8 × 14\nSum = 112\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
