      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can do this by dividing 91 by the smallest prime number, which is 2, and continuing with successive prime numbers until we can no longer divide evenly.\n\n91 ÷ 2 = 45.5 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 3 = 30.33 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 5 = 18.2 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 7 = 13 (divisible)\n\nSo, 91 = 7 × 13. Both 7 and 13 are prime numbers.\n\nNow, we can write the sum of all the positive divisors as the product of the sum of each prime factor raised to its respective power:\n\nSum of divisors = (7^1 - 1) × (13^1 - 1)\n\n= (7 - 1) × (13 - 1)\n\n= 6 × 12\n\n= 72\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 72.",
