    "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can do this by dividing 91 by the smallest prime number, which is 2. Since 91 is not divisible by 2, we move on to the next prime number, which is 3. Again, 91 is not divisible by 3. We continue this process until we find a prime number that divides 91. In this case, 91 is divisible by 7, giving us 91 = 7 * 13. Both 7 and 13 are prime numbers, so the prime factorization of 91 is 7 * 13.\n\nNow that we have the prime factorization, we can use it to find the sum of all the positive divisors. The formula for the sum of the divisors of a number n = p1^a1 * p2^a2 * ... * pk^ak is (1 + p1 + p1^2 + ... + p1^ak) * (1 + p2 + p2^2 + ... + p2^ak) * ... * (1 + pk + pk^2 + ... + pk^ak). In our case, n = 91, p1 = 7, a1 = 1, p2 = 13, and a2 = 1. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n(1 + 7 + 7^2) * (1 + 13 + 13^2) = (1 + 7 + 49) * (1 + 13 + 169) = 57 * 183 = 10311\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 10311.",
